<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Linux on Ondřej Honus' website</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/tags/linux/</link><description>Recent content in Linux on Ondřej Honus' website</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2026 11:30:59 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://ondrejhonus.com/tags/linux/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Rsync /home to drive</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/snippets/rsync-home/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2026 11:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/snippets/rsync-home/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Save exclude files to /var/tmp/ignorelist:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rubo77/rsync-homedir-excludes/master/rsync-homedir-excludes.txt -O /var/tmp/ignorelist
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have to mount your drive to /media/&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;/homebackup !&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rsync home folder to /media/&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;/backup:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo rsync -aP --exclude-from&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/var/tmp/ignorelist /home/$USER/ /media/$USER/homebackup
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Honest Opinions on Linux Distros</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/posts/distros-opinion/</link><pubDate>Thu, 19 Mar 2026 10:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/posts/distros-opinion/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="my-rating-of-linux-distros"&gt;My rating of Linux distros&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 id="1-void-linux"&gt;1. Void Linux&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Void linux is #1 only because it doesn&amp;rsquo;t use &lt;code&gt;systemd&lt;/code&gt; as an init system&amp;hellip; Okay also because of it&amp;rsquo;s blazingly fast package manager&amp;hellip; And customizability also &amp;gt;~&amp;lt;
I don&amp;rsquo;t know why, it might be because you build it to your needs, but I find it very snappy and comfortable to use. I for some reason really like it, and I can&amp;rsquo;t really explain why.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linux scheduled backup with CRON</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/scheduled-backup/</link><pubDate>Thu, 19 Mar 2026 10:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/scheduled-backup/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="python-script-to-backup"&gt;Python script to backup&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;backup.py&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; subprocess
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; len(sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;argv) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; print(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;No destination file provided&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;exit(&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;source &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;/home/u1/Plocha/&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;target &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;argv[&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;]
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;result &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; subprocess&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;run([&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;rsync&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;-av&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, source, target])
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; result&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;returncode &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; print(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Rsync backup was successful&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;exit(&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; print(&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;Error while backing up&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, result&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;returncode)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; sys&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;exit(&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="add-to-crontab"&gt;Add to crontab&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backup every day at 3:00&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sudo crontab -e
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-zsh" data-lang="zsh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# m h dom mon dow command&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; * * * /usr/bin/python3 /home/u1/backup.py /home/u1/backup/
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="reboot-every-monday-at-501"&gt;Reboot every monday at 5:01&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sudo crontab -e
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-zsh" data-lang="zsh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# m h dom mon dow command&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; * * &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; /bin/systemctl reboot
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Cool Linux tools</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/cool-commands/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 15:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/cool-commands/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="-a-terminal-based-file-manager"&gt;&amp;gt; A terminal based file manager&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;yazi
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;yazi&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-a-set-of-eyes-on-your-screen-that-follow-your-cursor-if-the-window-is-running-through-xwayland-good-way-to-check-wayland-compatibility"&gt;&amp;gt; A set of eyes on your screen that follow your cursor if the window is running through XWayland. Good way to check Wayland compatibility.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;xeyes
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;xeyes&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;xorg-xeyes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-terminal-that-has-built-in-image-compatibility-and-doesnt-require-weird-commands-for-using-ssh-and-stuff-like-kitty-does"&gt;&amp;gt; Terminal that has built in image compatibility, and doesnt require weird commands for using ssh and stuff like kitty does.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;foot
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;foot&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-tool-for-displaying-images-in-a-terminal-goes-well-with-foot"&gt;&amp;gt; Tool for displaying images in a terminal (goes well with &lt;code&gt;foot&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;chafa &amp;lt;image_file&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Package name: &lt;code&gt;chafa&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linux Basics</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/linux-basics/</link><pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 20:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/documents/linux-basics/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="exam-example"&gt;Exam example&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="part-1-basic-knowledge"&gt;Part 1: Basic knowledge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4 id="print-all-files-in-a-directory-including-hidden-files-permissions-group-and-user-owners"&gt;Print all files in a directory, including hidden files, permissions, group and user owners&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;ls -la /path/to/directory
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="print-first-15-lines-of-a-file"&gt;Print first 15 lines of a file&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;head -n &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt; /path/to/file
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="get-free-memory"&gt;Get free memory&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;free -h
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="show-disk-block-devices"&gt;Show disk block devices&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;lsblk
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="show-all-processes-running-under-root"&gt;Show all processes running under root&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;simple way (not 100% correct):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;ps aux | grep root
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;more correct way:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;ps -U root -u root
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="what-is-grub-and-what-is-it-for"&gt;What is GRUB and what is it for?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GRUB is a Linux bootloader. It&amp;rsquo;s responsible for loading the kernel, initializing the system and it provides a menu to select an operating system to boot.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Fix Distrobox xdg-open</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/snippets/distrobox-xdg-open/</link><pubDate>Mon, 16 Mar 2026 15:30:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/snippets/distrobox-xdg-open/</guid><description>&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 1. Clean broken paths to prevent &amp;#34;command not found&amp;#34; errors&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/xdg-open
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/distrobox-host-exec
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 2. Create the bridge in /usr/local/bin (High Priority Location)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo tee /usr/local/bin/xdg-open &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;lt; &amp;#39;EOF&amp;#39;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;#!/usr/bin/python3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;import sys, dbus, os
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;# Ensure the Host D-Bus is found
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;os.environ[&amp;#34;DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS&amp;#34;] = f&amp;#34;unix:path=/run/user/{os.getuid()}/bus&amp;#34;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;try:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; url = sys.argv[1]
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; bus = dbus.SessionBus()
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; obj = bus.get_object(&amp;#34;org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;/org/freedesktop/portal/desktop&amp;#34;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; iface = dbus.Interface(obj, &amp;#34;org.freedesktop.portal.OpenURI&amp;#34;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; iface.OpenURI(&amp;#34;&amp;#34;, url, {})
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;except Exception:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt; pass
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;EOF&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 3. Set execution permissions&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo chmod &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;755&lt;/span&gt; /usr/local/bin/xdg-open
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 4. Create Distrobox integration links&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo ln -sf /usr/local/bin/xdg-open /usr/local/bin/distrobox-host-exec
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 5. FIX FOR ICONS: Global Variable in /etc/environment&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# This ensures that GUI apps (like Antigravity) see the bridge even when opened via the menu&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;sudo sh -c &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;echo &amp;#39;BROWSER=\&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin/xdg-open\&amp;#34;&amp;#39; &amp;gt;&amp;gt; /etc/environment&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# 6. Update PATH for the current terminal session (Bash/Fish/Zsh)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;export PATH&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin:&lt;/span&gt;$PATH&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;export BROWSER&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin/xdg-open&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;hash -r 2&amp;gt;/dev/null &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; true
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;✅ Setup Finished! Testing...&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;xdg-open https://www.google.com
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# CREDIT: https://github.com/89luca89/distrobox/issues/1984&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>My Story With ThinkPads</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/posts/thinkpad-story/</link><pubDate>Sat, 24 Jan 2026 21:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/posts/thinkpad-story/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="how-i-got-into-thinkpads"&gt;How I Got Into Thinkpads&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been a Linux user for quite some time now, and it&amp;rsquo;s impossible to be a Linux die-hard without encountering ThinkPads. My journey with ThinkPads began several years ago when I got my first one, a ThinkPad T480.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="my-thinkpad-t480"&gt;My ThinkPad T480&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is where my ThinkPad adventure began. The T480 is an excellent laptop, in fact, I&amp;rsquo;m writing this part on it right now!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s built like a tank, but not a big tank, a relatively slim, portable tank (compared to the T420).
And it has a fantastic keyboard, as all older ThinkPads do.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Linux Distro Chooser</title><link>https://ondrejhonus.com/apps/distro-chooser/</link><pubDate>Sat, 24 Jan 2026 01:20:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://ondrejhonus.com/apps/distro-chooser/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="decide-on-the-perfect-linux-distro-for-you"&gt;Decide on the perfect Linux distro for you!&lt;/h2&gt;
